rent actives, which rely on individual exemptive orders.\n- UIT-structured ETFs (e.g., SPDR S&P 500 ETF Trust, SPDR Dow Jones Industrial Average ETF Trust), which rely on their own relief.\n- ETFs organized as share classes of mutual funds, which rely on separate relief.\n- Products outside the 1940 Act, such as commodity pools, which fall under the CEA and other regimes.\n\n**Rule 18f-4 interaction:** Leveraged and inverse funds using derivatives must either comply with the VaR test (relative or absolute) or qualify as limited derivatives users. Failure to comply affects eligibility regardless of 6c-11 status.\n\n*Caveat: My knowledge runs to June 2026, so verify the current rule text, any SEC staff relief, and 2026 developments with counsel.*","ttft_ms":8611,"type":"result","duration_ms":10457,"uuid":"974f22bd-b2bc-467b-8ad9-1a599b82b0bd","ttft_stream_ms":425,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":425,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
